{
    "background_story": "Colter Paine was a rugged outdoorsman who spent most of his life exploring the unforgiving wilderness of Alaska. A skilled mountaineer and hunter, he had faced countless challenges, from treacherous terrain to harsh weather conditions. But nothing could have prepared him for the pain he endured after a near-fatal accident on a solo expedition. Colter suffered a severe injury that left him with chronic pain and a long, arduous recovery. Despite the setbacks, he refused to give up, using his experience to help others navigate the wilderness safely. Colter's story became a testament to the human spirit's capacity for resilience and adaptation, as he transformed his pain into a catalyst for growth and a new sense of purpose.",
